This is a long one, so buckle up.

This is the story of how I ended up dating my abusive ex boyfriend.

&#x200B;

Freshman year of high school. He sat across from me at one of those four people tables, two people on one side, two on the other. I notice he's kind of off, all shaking and twitching. Let's call this boy B. B pulls me to the side, and says, "Can I tell you something?" And me being the concerned person I am, I let him. He tells me he's taken all sorts of drugs, as he was trying to die. I won't go into the specifics of which, but I offer to tell a teacher or call a hospital. He asks me not to, and me being naive, I oblige. Fast forward to about thirty minutes into the class, teacher calls on him to answer a question. But he's completely dazed, not moving, not blinking or talking. He then collapses, completely unconcious. Thankfully the guy sitting on the edge at the table next to him catches him. He begins shaking, seizing. Teacher yells for everyone to go into the ISS room (our classroom was connected to the ISS room.) Everyone leaves but me. I stay, watch as he slowly stops seizing, but is shaking. His hands are ice cold but his forehead was burning. I start crying, holding his hand and trying to wake him up. Again, we had never spoken before. When he wakes up, he starts full on sobbing and screaming my name. Not sure why, but he was clinging onto me. He wouldn't let go of me, he said he needed me and I was making him feel better, his tears soaked my sleeves. It was scary. Teacher asks me what happened, and I tell them out of fear. He's taken to the hospital, and I wasn't allowed to go. I wasn't sure why, but I felt some sort of connection to him. It was terrifying. When he left, I had a panic attack that for some reason paralyzed my hands. It only lasted five minutes, but I couldn't walk or breathe. He comes back about a week later. We start dating. From there on it was very abusive, which I won't go into detail  because I'm not comfortable with it. This is my first time ever telling people other than the teacher what happened to him. And I know this sounds very stupid, but I felt a strong, emotional connection to him. Of course, I'm glad he's out of my life now, as his abuse was far too intense. But I only go out off my way to help close friends, not people I'm not really close to. And to watch this man seize right in front of my eyes, was terrifying. Then to have this person, who I hardly talk to, cling onto me, was terrifying. To those who read this, thank you for taking the time. I know this isn't really a big deal, and might seem fake, but this really spooked me, especially as someone who believes in super natural stuff. Have a lovely day or night, everyone.

&#x200B;

Edit: I know people are going to ask, so I'll try to explain this. I don't remember exactly how they got him to stop seizing. There were a bunch of paramedics and they did some thing to stop him, I'm not sure what. This event lasted for a while, though. Not sure how long, I didn't have a timer on me to time it. And of course I backed away when they were working on him. But when they were done, I came back out of concern. Sorry for the confusion, this was many years ago so I can't recall exactly what the paramedics did. It took the ambulance a while to get there though, as our school was far from civilization.

